update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$Choice C is correct. The given equation ax + by = b can be rewritten in slope-intercept form, y = mx + k, where m represents the slope of the line represented by the equation, and k represents the y-coordinate of the y-intercept of the line. Subtracting ax from both sides of the equation yields by = -ax + b, and dividing both sides of this equation by b yields y = -a/b x + b/b, or y = -a/b x + 1. With the equation now in slope-intercept form, it shows that k = 1, which means the y-coordinate of the y-intercept is 1. It’s given that a and b are both greater than 0 (positive) and that a < b. Since m = -a/b, the slope of the line must be a value between -1 and 0. Choice C is the only graph of a line that has a y-value of the y-intercept that is 1 and a slope that is between -1 and 0.
Choices A, B, and D are incorrect because the slopes of the lines in these graphs aren’t between -1 and 0.$qb$ from questions q where q.id = k.question_id and q.source_ref = 'CB-0b46bad5' and left(md5(q.stem), 8) = '167d76c0';
