update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$Choice C is correct. The given equation is quadratic. The maximum value of a function defined by a quadratic equation can be displayed as a constant in the vertex form of the equation, f(x) = a(x - h)^(2) + k, where the maximum value of the function is k, which occurs when x = h, and a is a constant. The given equation can be rewritten in this form by completing the square. To complete the square, the given equation can be rewritten as f(x) = -6(x^(2) - 10x) - 126, which is equivalent to f(x) = -6(x^(2) - 10x + 25) - 126 + 6(25), or f(x) = -6(x - 5)^(2) + 24. This equation is in vertex form, where a = -6, h = 5, and k = 24. Therefore, f(x) = -6(x - 5)^(2) + 24 displays the maximum value, 24, of the function as a constant.
Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.
Choice B is incorrect. This form displays one of the zeros, not the maximum value, of the function as a constant.
Choice D is incorrect. This form displays the zeros, not the maximum value, of the function as constants.$qb$ from questions q where q.id = k.question_id and q.source_ref = 'CB-16aa9758' and left(md5(q.stem), 8) = '59369662';
