update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$Choice D is correct. The value of p(12) depends on the value of the constant c, so the value of c must first be determined. It is given that p(c) = 10. Based on the definition of p, it follows that:
p(c) = ((c - c)^(2) + 160)/2c = 10
160/2c = 10
2c = 16
c = 8
This means that p(x) = ((x - 8)^(2) + 160)/16 for all values of x. Therefore:
p(12) = ((12 - 8)^(2) + 160)/16
= (16 + 160)/16
= 11
Choice A is incorrect. It is the value of p(8), not p(12). Choices B and C are incorrect. If one of these values were correct, then x = 12 and the selected value of p(12) could be substituted into the equation to solve for c. However, the values of c that result from choices B and C each result in p(c) < 10.$qb$ from questions q where q.id = k.question_id and q.source_ref = 'CB-1a722d7d' and left(md5(q.stem), 8) = '0bd6240f';
