update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$The correct answer is 28. The equation of a circle in the xy-plane can be written as (x - t)^(2) + (y - s)^(2) = r^(2), where the center of the circle is (t, s) and the radius of the circle is r. It’s given that circle A is defined by the equation x^(2) + (y - 6)^(2) = 7, which can be written as (x - 0)^(2) + (y - 6)^(2) = (√7)^(2). It follows that r = √7 and the radius of circle A is √7. It’s also given that circle B has the same radius as circle A. If the equation of circle B is (x - h)^(2) + (y - k)^(2) = a, then a = r^(2). Substituting √7 for r in this equation yields a = (√7)^(2), or a = 7. It follows that the value of 4a is 4(7), or 28.$qb$ from questions q where q.id = k.question_id and q.source_ref = 'CB-1b2b20b9' and left(md5(q.stem), 8) = 'a2db7e43';
