update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$Choice A is correct. For positive values of a, a^(m)/a^(n) = a^(m - n), where m and n are integers. Since it's given that h > 0 and q > 0, this property can be applied to rewrite the given expression as (h^(15 - 5))(q^(7 - 21)), which is equivalent to h^(10)q^(-14). For positive values of a, a^(-n) = 1/a^(n). This property can be applied to rewrite the expression h^(10)q^(-14) as (h^(10))(1/q^(14)), which is equivalent to h^(10)/q^(14).
Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.
Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.
