update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$Choice D is correct. Since x^(3) - 9x = x(x + 3)(x - 3) and x^(2) - 2x - 3 = (x + 1)(x - 3), the fraction (f(x))/(g(x)) can be written as (x(x + 3)(x - 3))/((x + 1)(x - 3)). It is given that x > 3, so the common factor x - 3 is not equal to 0. Therefore, the fraction can be further simplified to (x(x + 3))/(x + 1).
Choice A is incorrect. The expression 1/(x + 1) is not equivalent to (f(x))/(g(x)) because at x = 0, 1/(x + 1) as a value of 1 and (f(x))/(g(x)) has a value of 0.
Choice B is incorrect and results from omitting the factor x in the factorization of f(x). Choice C is incorrect and may result from incorrectly factoring g(x) as (x + 1)(x + 3) instead of (x + 1)(x - 3).$qb$ from questions q where q.id = k.question_id and q.source_ref = 'CB-22fd3e1f' and left(md5(q.stem), 8) = '1d00a521';
