update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$Choice A is correct. A circle has 360 degrees of arc. In the circle shown, O is the center of the circle and ∠AOC is a central angle of the circle. From the figure, the two diameters that meet to form ∠AOC are perpendicular, so the measure of ∠AOC is 90°. Therefore, the length of minor arc AC is 90/360 of the circumference of the circle. Since the circumference of the circle is 36, the length of minor arc AC is 90/360 (36) = 9.
Choices B, C, and D are incorrect. The perpendicular diameters divide the circumference of the circle into four equal arcs; therefore, minor arc AC is 1/4 of the circumference. However, the lengths in choices B and C are, respectively, 1/3 and 1/2 the circumference of the circle, and the length in choice D is the length of the entire circumference. None of these lengths is 1/4 the circumference.$qb$ from questions q where q.id = k.question_id and q.source_ref = 'CB-23c5fcce' and left(md5(q.stem), 8) = '78d1d063';
