update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$Choice A is correct. To write the formula as T in terms of m, v, and L means to isolate T on one side of the equation. First, multiply both sides of the equation by m, which gives mv^(2) = mLT/m, which simplifies to mv^(2)= LT. Next, divide both sides of the equation by L, which gives mv^(2)/L = LT/L, which simplifies to T = mv^(2)/L.
