update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$Choice B is correct. Adding y to each side of the second equation in the given system of equations yields 8x + 16 = y. Substituting 8x + 16 for y in the first equation yields x^(2) + 8x + 16 + 10 = 10. Subtracting 10 from each side of this equation yields x^(2) + 8x + 16 = 0. This equation can be rewritten as (x + 4)^(2) = 0. Taking the square root of each side of this equation yields x + 4 = 0. Subtracting 4 from each side of this equation yields x = -4. Therefore, the value of x is -4.
