update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$Choice B is correct. The sine of any acute angle is equal to the cosine of its complement. It’s given that in right triangle RST, the sum of the measures of angle R and angle S is 90 degrees. Therefore, angle R and angle S are complementary, and the value of sin R is equal to the value of cos S. It's given that the value of sin R is √15/4, so the value of cos S is also √15/4.
