update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$Choice B is correct. The sum of the interior angles of a triangle is 180°. The measures of the two interior angles of the given triangle are shown. Therefore, the measure of the third interior angle is 180° – 70° – 50° = 60°. The angles of measures x° and 60° are supplementary, so their sum is 180°. Therefore, x = 180 – 60 = 120.
