update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$Choice C is correct. If the equation is true for all x, then the expressions on both sides of the equation will be equivalent. Multiplying the polynomials on the left-hand side of the equation gives 5ax^(3) - abx^(2) + 4ax + 15x^(2) - 3bx + 12. On the right-hand side of the equation, the only x^(2)-term is -9x^(2). Since the expressions on both sides of the equation are equivalent, it follows that -abx^(2) + 15x^(2) = -9x^(2), which can be rewritten as (-ab + 15)x^(2) = -9x^(2). Therefore, -ab + 15 = -9, which gives ab = 24.
