update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$Choice C is correct. It’s given that triangle XYZ is similar to triangle RST, such that X, Y, and Z correspond to R, S, and T, respectively. Since corresponding angles of similar triangles are congruent, it follows that the measure of ∠Z is congruent to the measure of ∠T. It’s given that the measure of ∠Z is 20°. Therefore, the measure of ∠T is 20°.
Choice A is incorrect and may result from a conceptual error.
Choice B is incorrect. This is half the measure of ∠Z.
Choice D is incorrect. This is twice the measure of ∠Z.$qb$ from questions q where q.id = k.question_id and q.source_ref = 'CB-3b225698' and left(md5(q.stem), 8) = '9ac4cf52';
