update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$Choice A is correct. The value of k can be found using the slope-intercept form of a linear equation, y = mx + b, where m is the slope and b is the y-coordinate of the y-intercept. The equation ax + ky = 6 can be rewritten in the form y = -ax/k + 6/k. One of the given points, (0, -3), is the y-intercept. Thus, the y-coordinate of the y-intercept -3 must be equal to 6/k. Multiplying both sides by k gives -3k = 6. Dividing both sides by -3 gives k = -2.
Choices B, C, and D are incorrect and may result from errors made rewriting the given equation.$qb$ from questions q where q.id = k.question_id and q.source_ref = 'CB-3cdbf026' and left(md5(q.stem), 8) = 'dd24aeb0';
