update question_options o set body = $qb$I and III only$qb$, image_url = null from questions q where q.id = o.question_id and o.label = 'D' and q.source_ref = 'CB-3f8a701b' and left(md5(q.stem), 8) = '93d3c5ea';
update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$Choice D is correct. For a linear equation in a form ax + b = cx + d to have no solutions, the x-terms must have equal coefficients and the remaining terms must not be equal. Expanding the right-hand side of the given equation yields 9x + 5 = ax + ab. Inspecting the x-terms, 9 must equal a, so statement I must be true. Inspecting the remaining terms, 5 can’t equal 9b. Dividing both of these quantities by 9 yields that b can’t equal 5/9. Therefore, statement III must be true. Since b can have any value other than 5/9, statement II may or may not be true.
Choice A is incorrect. For the given equation to have no solution, both a = 9 and b ≠ 5/9 must be true. Choice B is incorrect because it must also be true that b ≠ 5/9. Choice C is incorrect because when a = 9, there are many values of b that lead to an equation having no solution. That is, b might be 5, but b isn’t required to be 5.$qb$ from questions q where q.id = k.question_id and q.source_ref = 'CB-3f8a701b' and left(md5(q.stem), 8) = '93d3c5ea';
update questions set stem = $qb$The equation 9x + 5 = a(x + b), where a and b are constants, has no solutions. Which of the following must be true?
I. a = 9
II. b = 5
III. b ≠ 5/9$qb$, image_url = null, updated_at = now() where source_ref = 'CB-3f8a701b' and left(md5(stem), 8) = '93d3c5ea';
update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$The correct answer is 8. The mean of a data set is the sum of the values in the data set divided by the number of values in the data set. It's given in the table that the times, in minutes, it took Robert to complete each of the tasks are 5, 2, 15, 9, and 9. The sum of these times is 5 + 2 + 15 + 9 + 9, or 40, minutes. There are 5 tasks in the project. Therefore, the mean time, in minutes, for Robert to complete a task for this project is 40 ÷ 5, or 8.$qb$ from questions q where q.id = k.question_id and q.source_ref = 'CB-40f0ee70' and left(md5(q.stem), 8) = 'a2db7e43';
