update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$Choice A is correct. It is given that the relationship between population and year is linear; therefore, the function that models the population t years after 2000 is of the form P(t) = mt + b, where m is the slope and b is the population when t = 0. In the year 2000, t = 0. Therefore, b = 862. The slope is given by m = (P(10) - P(0))/(10 - 0) = (846 - 862)/(10 - 0) = (-16)/10 = -1.6. Therefore, P(t) = -1.6t + 862, which is equivalent to the equation in choice A.
Choice B is incorrect and may be the result of incorrectly calculating the slope as just the change in the value of P. Choice C is incorrect and may be the result of the same error as in choice B, in addition to incorrectly using t to represent the year, instead of the number of years after 2000. Choice D is incorrect and may be the result of incorrectly using t to represent the year instead of the number of years after 2000.$qb$ from questions q where q.id = k.question_id and q.source_ref = 'CB-41fdc0b8' and left(md5(q.stem), 8) = '8d425b8c';
