update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$Choice D is correct. It’s given that 2x^(2) + ax is equivalent to x(2x + 7) for some constant a. Distributing the x over each term in the parentheses gives 2x^(2) + 7x, which is in the same form as the first given expression, 2x^(2) + ax. The coefficient of the second term in 2x^(2) + 7x is 7. Therefore, the value of a is 7.
Choice A is incorrect. If the value of a were 2, then 2x^(2) + ax would be equivalent to 2x^(2) + 2x, which isn’t equivalent to x(2x + 7). Choice B is incorrect. If the value of a were 3, then 2x^(2) + ax would be equivalent to 2x^(2) + 3x, which isn’t equivalent to x(2x + 7). Choice C is incorrect. If the value of a were 4, then 2x^(2) + ax would be equivalent to 2x^(2) + 4x, which isn’t equivalent to x(2x + 7).$qb$ from questions q where q.id = k.question_id and q.source_ref = 'CB-49efde89' and left(md5(q.stem), 8) = '007b365e';
