update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$Choice B is correct. It’s given that triangle LMN is similar to triangle PQR. Corresponding angles of similar triangles are congruent. Since angle M and angle Q correspond to each other, they must be congruent. Therefore, if the measure of angle M is 53°, then the measure of angle Q is also 53°.
Choice A is incorrect and may result from concluding that angle M and angle Q are complementary rather than congruent.
Choice C is incorrect and may result from concluding that angle M and angle Q are supplementary rather than congruent.
Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.$qb$ from questions q where q.id = k.question_id and q.source_ref = 'CB-4ff7b652' and left(md5(q.stem), 8) = '7db37d97';
