update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$The correct answer is 44. For a function defined by an equation of the form f(x) = a(1 + r/100)^(x/k), where a, r, and k are positive constants, the value of f(x) increases by r% for every increase of x by k. The given equation can be rewritten as f(x) = 27(1.20)^(2x/6), or f(x) = 27((1.2)^(2))^(x/6), which is equivalent to f(x) = 27(1.44)^(x/6), or f(x) = 27(1 + 44/100)^(x/6). This equation is of the form f(x) = a(1 + r/100)^(x/k), where a = 27, r = 44, and k = 6. It follows that the value of f(x) increases by 44% for every increase of x by 6. Therefore, the value of p is 44.
Alternate approach: It's given that f(x) = 27(1.20)^(x/3). An increase in the value of x by 6 can be represented by the expression x + 6. The value of f(x + 6) can be found by substituting x + 6 for x in the equation f(x) = 27(1.20)^(x/3), which yields f(x + 6) = 27(1.20)^((x + 6)/3). By the product property of exponents, this equation is equivalent to f(x + 6) = 27(1.20)^(x/3) · (1.20)^(6/3), or f(x + 6) = 27(1.20)^(x/3) · (1.20)^(2), which can be rewritten as f(x + 6) = 27(1.20)^(x/3) · (1.44). Since f(x) = 27(1.20)^(x/3), it follows that f(x + 6) = f(x) · (1.44). Therefore, for any value of x, the value of f(x + 6) is 1.44 times, or 44% greater than, the value of f(x). It's given that the value of f(x) increases by p% for every increase in the value of x by 6. It follows that the value of p is 44.$qb$ from questions q where q.id = k.question_id and q.source_ref = 'CB-512bd5b4' and left(md5(q.stem), 8) = '2fcb9ea4';
