update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$Choice B is correct. Subtracting 4 from each side of the given equation yields 6 = 2x, or x = 3, so the equation has a unique solution of x = 3.
Choice A is incorrect. Since 3 is a value of x that satisfies the given equation, the equation has at least 1 solution. Choice C is incorrect. Linear equations can have 0, 1, or infinitely many solutions; no linear equation has exactly 3 solutions. Choice D is incorrect. If a linear equation has infinitely many solutions, it can be reduced to 0 = 0. This equation reduces to x = 3, so there is only 1 solution.$qb$ from questions q where q.id = k.question_id and q.source_ref = 'CB-550b352c' and left(md5(q.stem), 8) = 'ebb7b7a8';
