update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$Choice D is correct. In the given equation, x(r - 9) + 4 = 19x + 27, r is a positive integer. Distributing on the left-hand side of this equation yields rx - 9x + 4 = 19x + 27. Subtracting 4 from both sides of this equation yields rx - 9x = 19x + 23. Subtracting 19x from both sides of this equation yields rx - 28x = 23, which can be written as (r - 28)x = 23. For this equation to have exactly one solution, the coefficient of x, (r - 28), cannot be equal to 0. Therefore, 28 CANNOT be the value of r.
Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.
