update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$The correct answer is 175. It's given that line g is parallel to line h. Since line l intersects both lines, it's a transversal. The angles in the figure marked as 175° and x° are on the same side of the transversal, where one is an interior angle with line h as a side, and the other is an exterior angle with line g as a side, respectively. Thus, the marked angles are corresponding angles. When two parallel lines are intersected by a transversal, corresponding angles have equal measure. Therefore, the value of x is 175.$qb$ from questions q where q.id = k.question_id and q.source_ref = 'CB-58687a66' and left(md5(q.stem), 8) = '02fc3b26';
update questions set stem = $qb$In the figure shown, line g is parallel to line h. Line 𝓁 intersects both lines. What is the value of x?$qb$, image_url = $qb$/question-figures/cb/CB-58687a66.png$qb$, updated_at = now() where source_ref = 'CB-58687a66' and left(md5(stem), 8) = '02fc3b26';
update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$The correct answer is -10. Adding y to both sides of the second equation in the given system yields 20x + 100 = y. Substituting 20x + 100 for y in the first equation in the given system yields x^(2) + 20x + 100 + 7 = 7. Subtracting 7 from both sides of this equation yields x^(2) + 20x + 100 = 0. Factoring the left-hand side of this equation yields (x + 10)(x + 10) = 0, or (x + 10)^(2) = 0. Taking the square root of both sides of this equation yields x + 10 = 0. Subtracting 10 from both sides of this equation yields x = -10. Therefore, the value of x is -10.$qb$ from questions q where q.id = k.question_id and q.source_ref = 'CB-58b109d4' and left(md5(q.stem), 8) = '7daf0378';
