update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$Choice A is correct. In 1 year, there are 4 quarter years, so the number of quarter years, q, is 4 times the number of years, t; that is, q = 4t. This is equivalent to t = q/4, and substituting this into the expression for M in terms of t gives M = 1,800(1.02)^(q/4).
Choices B and D are incorrect and may be the result of incorrectly using t = 4q instead of q = 4t. (Choices B and D are nearly the same since 1.02^(4q) is equivalent to (1.02^(4))^(q), which is approximately 1.082^(q) .) Choice C is incorrect and may be the result of incorrectly using t = 4q and unnecessarily dividing 0.02 by 4.$qb$ from questions q where q.id = k.question_id and q.source_ref = 'CB-59d1f4b5' and left(md5(q.stem), 8) = '9e49131c';
