update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$Choice C is correct. Applying the distributive property to the given expression yields d(8d^(2) - 3) - 6(8d^(2) - 3). Applying the distributive property once again to this expression yields (d)(8d^(2)) + (d)(-3) + (-6)(8d^(2)) + (-6)(-3), or 8d^(3) + (-3d) + (-48d^(2)) + 18. This expression can be rewritten as 8d^(3) - 48d^(2) - 3d + 18. Thus, (d - 6)(8d^(2) - 3) is equivalent to 8d^(3) - 48d^(2) - 3d + 18.
