update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$Choice C is correct. This exponential growth model can be written in the form p(t) = A(1 + r)^(t), where p(t) is the population t years after 1788, A is the initial population, and r is the yearly growth rate, expressed as a decimal. Since there were 24 jackrabbits in Australia in 1788, A = 24. Since the number of jackrabbits increased by an average of 16.2% each year, r = 0.162. Therefore, the equation that best models this situation is p(t) = 24(1.162)^(t).
