update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$Choice B is correct. A cube has 6 faces of equal area, so if the total surface area of a cube is 6(a/4)^(2), then the area of one face is (a/4)^(2). Likewise, the area of one face of a cube is the square of one of its edges; therefore, if the area of one face is (a/4)^(2), then the length of one edge of the cube is a/4. Since the perimeter of one face of a cube is four times the length of one edge, the perimeter is 4(a/4) = a.
Choice A is incorrect because if the perimeter of one face of the cube is a/4, then the total surface area of the cube is 6((a/4)/4)^(2) = 6(a/16)^(2), which is not 6(a/4)^(2). Choice C is incorrect because if the perimeter of one face of the cube is 4a, then the total surface area of the cube is 6(4a/4)^(2) = 6a^(2), which is not 6(a/4)^(2). Choice D is incorrect because if the perimeter of one face of the cube is 6a, then the total surface area of the cube is 6(6a/4)^(2) = 6(3a/2)^(2), which is not 6(a/4)^(2).$qb$ from questions q where q.id = k.question_id and q.source_ref = 'CB-635f54ee' and left(md5(q.stem), 8) = '83f23a30';
