update question_options o set body = $qb$880$qb$, image_url = null from questions q where q.id = o.question_id and o.label = 'D' and q.source_ref = 'CB-6676f055' and left(md5(q.stem), 8) = '1793fe26';
update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$Choice C is correct. The function f is quadratic, so it will have either a maximum or a minimum at the vertex of the graph. Since the coefficient of the quadratic term (–0.28) is negative, the vertex will be at a maximum. The equation f(θ) = –0.28(θ – 27)^(2) + 880 is given in vertex form, so the vertex is at θ = 27. Therefore, an angle of 27 degrees gives the greatest airflow.
Choices A and B are incorrect and may be the result of misidentifying which value in a quadratic equation in vertex form represents the vertex. Choice D is incorrect. This choice identifies the maximum value of f(θ) rather than the value of θ for which f(θ) is maximized.$qb$ from questions q where q.id = k.question_id and q.source_ref = 'CB-6676f055' and left(md5(q.stem), 8) = '1793fe26';
update questions set stem = $qb$f(θ) = -0.28(θ - 27)^(2) + 880
An engineer wanted to identify the best angle for a cooling fan in an engine in order to get the greatest airflow. The engineer discovered that the function above models the airflow f(θ), in cubic feet per minute, as a function of the angle of the fan θ, in degrees. According to the model, what angle, in degrees, gives the greatest airflow?$qb$, image_url = null, updated_at = now() where source_ref = 'CB-6676f055' and left(md5(stem), 8) = '1793fe26';
update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$The correct answer is -12. It’s given that function f is a quadratic function where f(-20) = 0 and f(-4) = 0. It follows that the graph of y = f(x) in the xy-plane passes through the points (-20, 0) and (-4, 0). When the graph of a quadratic function contains two points (a, 0) and (b, 0), the x-coordinate of the vertex of the graph is the average of a and b. Therefore, the x-coordinate of the vertex of the graph of y = f(x) is (-20 + (-4))/2, or -12. It's given that the graph of y = f(x) in the xy-plane has a vertex at (r, -64). It follows that the value of r is -12.$qb$ from questions q where q.id = k.question_id and q.source_ref = 'CB-668f1863' and left(md5(q.stem), 8) = '978da778';
