update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$Choice B is correct. The graph of a quadratic function in the xy-plane is a parabola. The axis of symmetry of the parabola passes through the vertex of the parabola. Therefore, the vertex of the parabola and the midpoint of the segment between the two x-intercepts of the graph have the same x-coordinate. Since f(-3) = f(-1) = 0, the x-coordinate of the vertex is (-3 + (-1))/2 = -2. Of the shown intervals, only the interval in choice B contains –2. Choices A, C, and D are incorrect and may result from either calculation errors or misidentification of the graph’s x-intercepts.$qb$ from questions q where q.id = k.question_id and q.source_ref = 'CB-70753f99' and left(md5(q.stem), 8) = 'bb00cefb';
