update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$Choice C is correct. First, M̅P̅ is the hypotenuse of right △MNP, whose legs have lengths 3 and 4. Therefore, (MP)^(2) = 3^(2) + 4^(2), so (MP)^(2) = 25 and MP = 5. Second, because ∠MNP corresponds to ∠NQP and because ∠MPN corresponds to ∠NPQ, △MNP is similar to △NQP. The ratio of corresponding sides of similar triangles is constant, so NQ/MN = NP/MP. Since MP = 5 and it’s given that MN = 3 and NP = 4, NQ/3 = 4/5. Solving for NQ results in NQ = 12/5, or 2.4.
Choices A, B, and D are incorrect and may result from setting up incorrect ratios.$qb$ from questions q where q.id = k.question_id and q.source_ref = 'CB-740bf79f' and left(md5(q.stem), 8) = 'ec1761d5';
