update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$Choice D is correct. In the figure, it’s given that segment AD is perpendicular to line l at point A. Statement I is that segment AD is perpendicular to line m at point D. It follows that angles BAC and EDC are right angles. Therefore, triangles ABC and DEC are right triangles. At least one pair of congruent corresponding sides is needed to determine triangle congruence by the side-angle-side (SAS) condition or the angle-side-angle (ASA) condition, so statement I is not sufficient to determine that triangle ABC is congruent to triangle DEC. Statement II is that AC = 13 and DC = 13. It follows that triangles ABC and DEC share one pair of congruent corresponding sides. Two additional pairs of congruent corresponding parts are needed to determine triangle congruence by SAS condition, ASA condition, or side-side-side (SSS) condition, so statement II is not sufficient to determine that triangle ABC is congruent to triangle DEC. Therefore, neither I nor II is sufficient by itself to determine that triangle ABC is congruent to triangle DEC.
Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.
Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.
