update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$Choice B is correct. Any line in the xy-plane can be defined by an equation in the form y = mx + b, where m is the slope of the line and b is the y-coordinate of the y-intercept of the line. From the graph, the y-intercept of the line is (0, 3). Therefore, b = 3. The slope of the line is the change in the value of y divided by the change in the value of x for any two points on the line. The line shown passes through (0, 3) and (1, 0), so m = (3 - 0)/(0 - 1), or m = –3. Therefore, the equation of the line is y = –3x + 3.
Choices A and C are incorrect because the equations given in these choices represent a line with a positive slope. However, the line shown has a negative slope. Choice D is incorrect because the equation given in this choice represents a line with slope of -1/3. However, the line shown has a slope of –3.$qb$ from questions q where q.id = k.question_id and q.source_ref = 'CB-8a1544f1' and left(md5(q.stem), 8) = '46c7c52b';
