update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$Choice A is correct. The mean of a data set is the sum of the values divided by the number of values. The mean of data set A is 45/9, or 5. The mean of data set B is 145/10, or 14.5. Thus, the means are different. The median of a data set is the middle value when the values are ordered from least to greatest. The medians of data sets A and B are both 5. Therefore, the medians are the same, so only the means are different.
Choices B, C, and D are incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.$qb$ from questions q where q.id = k.question_id and q.source_ref = 'CB-9110c120' and left(md5(q.stem), 8) = '19f1416c';
