update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$The correct answer is 45. An isosceles right triangle has a right angle and two legs of equal length. In the triangle shown, one angle is a right angle and the two legs each have a length of 15. Thus, the given triangle is an isosceles right triangle. In an isosceles right triangle, the measures of the two non-right angles are 45°. It follows that the value of x is 45.$qb$ from questions q where q.id = k.question_id and q.source_ref = 'CB-9823f279' and left(md5(q.stem), 8) = '258f4ef7';
