update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$Choice C is correct. Since lines l and k are parallel, corresponding angles formed by the intersection of line j with lines l and k are congruent. Therefore, the angle with measure a° must be the supplement of the angle with measure 64°. The sum of two supplementary angles is 180°, so a = 180 – 64 = 116.
