update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$Choice B is correct. Since it's given that P is the center of a circle with a radius of 9 inches, and that points Q and R lie on that circle, it follows that P̅Q̅ and R̅P̅ of triangle PQR each have a length of 9 inches. Let the length of Q̅R̅ be x inches. It follows that the perimeter of triangle PQR is 9 + 9 + x inches. Since it's given that the perimeter of triangle PQR is 31 inches, it follows that 9 + 9 + x = 31, or 18 + x = 31. Subtracting 18 from both sides of this equation gives x = 13. Therefore, the length, in inches, of Q̅R̅ is 13.
Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.
Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.
