update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$Choice A is correct. Since (x^(2) - x) is a common term in the original expression, like terms can be added: 2(x^(2) - x) + 3(x^(2) - x) = 5(x^(2) - x). Distributing the constant term 5 yields 5x^(2) - 5x.
Choice B is incorrect and may result from not distributing the negative signs in the expressions within the parentheses. Choice C is incorrect and may result from not distributing the negative signs in the expressions within the parentheses and from incorrectly eliminating the x^(2)-term. Choice D is incorrect and may result from incorrectly eliminating the x-term.$qb$ from questions q where q.id = k.question_id and q.source_ref = 'CB-9ed9f54d' and left(md5(q.stem), 8) = 'aac79ee6';
