update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$Choice D is correct. It's given that in triangle ABC, the measure of angle B is 90° and B̅D̅ is an altitude of the triangle. Therefore, the measure of angle BDC is 90°. It follows that angle B is congruent to angle D and angle C is congruent to angle C. By the angle-angle similarity postulate, triangle ABC is similar to triangle BDC. Since triangles ABC and BDC are similar, it follows that AC/AB = BC/BD. It's also given that the length of A̅B̅ is 15 and the length of A̅C̅ is 23 greater than the length of A̅B̅. Therefore, the length of A̅C̅ is 15 + 23, or 38. Substituting 15 for AB and 38 for AC in the equation AC/AB = BC/BD yields 38/15 = BC/BD. Therefore, the value of BC/BD is 38/15.
Choice A is incorrect. This is the value of BD/BC.
Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.
Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.$qb$ from questions q where q.id = k.question_id and q.source_ref = 'CB-a0369739' and left(md5(q.stem), 8) = 'd9cc5a7a';
