update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$Choice C is correct. The expression can be written as a difference of squares x^(2) – y^(2), which can be factored as (x + y)(x – y). Here, y^(2) = 5, so y = √5, and the expression therefore factors as (x + √5)(x - √5).
Choices A and B are incorrect and may result from misunderstanding how to factor a difference of squares. Choice D is incorrect; (x + 5)(x – 1) can be rewritten as x^(2) + 4x – 5, which is not equivalent to the original expression.$qb$ from questions q where q.id = k.question_id and q.source_ref = 'CB-a05bd3a4' and left(md5(q.stem), 8) = 'c637d07e';
