update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$Choice D is correct. Factoring out the coefficient 1/3, the given expression can be rewritten as 1/3 (x^(2) - 6). The expression x^(2) - 6 can be approached as a difference of squares and rewritten as (x - √6)(x + √6). Therefore, k must be √6.
Choice A is incorrect. If k were 2, then the expression given would be rewritten as 1/3 (x - 2)(x + 2), which is equivalent to 1/3 x^(2) - 4/3, not 1/3 x^(2) - 2.
Choice B is incorrect. This may result from incorrectly factoring the expression and finding (x - 6)(x + 6) as the factored form of the expression. Choice C is incorrect. This may result from incorrectly distributing the 1/3 and rewriting the expression as 1/3 (x^(2) - 2).$qb$ from questions q where q.id = k.question_id and q.source_ref = 'CB-a0b4103e' and left(md5(q.stem), 8) = '71891b09';
