update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$The correct answer is 192. The measure of an angle, in degrees, can be found by multiplying its measure, in radians, by (180 degrees)/(π radians). Multiplying the given angle measure, 16π/15 radians, by (180 degrees)/(π radians) yields (16π/15 radians)((180 degrees)/πradians), which simplifies to 192 degrees.$qb$ from questions q where q.id = k.question_id and q.source_ref = 'CB-a0cacec1' and left(md5(q.stem), 8) = '3d714ef1';
