update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$Choice B is correct. It’s given that x^(2) = a + b and y^(2) = a + c. Using the distributive property, the expression (x^(2) - y^(2))^(2) can be rewritten as (x^(2))^(2) - 2x^(2)y^(2) + (y^(2))^(2). Substituting a + b and a + c for x^(2) and y^(2), respectively, in this expression yields (a + b)^(2) - 2((a + b)(a + c)) + (a + c)^(2). Expanding this expression yields (a^(2) + 2ab + b^(2)) - (2a^(2) + 2bc + 2ac + 2ab) + (a^(2) + 2ac + c^(2)). Combining like terms, this expression can be rewritten as b^(2) - 2bc + c^(2).
Choices A, C, and D are incorrect and may result from an error in using the distributive property, substituting, or combining like terms.$qb$ from questions q where q.id = k.question_id and q.source_ref = 'CB-a255ae72' and left(md5(q.stem), 8) = 'de42c98a';
