update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$Choice C is correct. The total volume of the cylindrical can is found by multiplying the area of the base of the can, 75 square cm, by the height of the can, 10 cm, which yields 750 cubic cm. If the syrup needed to fill the can has a volume of 110 cubic cm, then the remaining volume for the pieces of
fruit is 750 - 110 = 640 cubic cm.
Choice A is incorrect because if the fruit had a volume of 7.5 cubic cm, there would be 750 - 7.5 = 742.5 cubic cm of syrup needed to fill the can to the top. Choice B is incorrect because if the fruit had a volume of 185 cubic cm, there would be 750 - 185 = 565 cubic cm of syrup needed to fill the can to the top. Choice D is incorrect because it is the total volume of the can, not just of the pieces of fruit.$qb$ from questions q where q.id = k.question_id and q.source_ref = 'CB-a2e76b60' and left(md5(q.stem), 8) = '8703fec6';
