Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.$qb$ from questions q where q.id = k.question_id and q.source_ref = 'CB-a456f28c' and left(md5(q.stem), 8) = 'a2db7e43';
update questions set stem = $qb$In the figure, two lines intersect at a point. Angle 1 and angle 2 are vertical angles. The measure of angle 1 is 72°. What is the measure of angle 2?$qb$, image_url = $qb$/question-figures/cb/CB-a456f28c.png$qb$, updated_at = now() where source_ref = 'CB-a456f28c' and left(md5(stem), 8) = 'a2db7e43';
update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$The correct answer is 5. It’s given that f(x) = -a^(x) + b. Substituting -a^(x) + b for f(x) in the equation y = f(x) - 15 yields y = -a^(x) + b - 15. It’s given that the y-intercept of the graph of y = f(x) - 15 is (0, -99/7). Substituting 0 for x and -99/7 for y in the equation y = -a^(x) + b - 15 yields -99/7 = -a^(0) + b - 15, which is equivalent to -99/7 = -1 + b - 15, or -99/7 = b - 16. Adding 16 to both sides of this equation yields 13/7 = b. It’s given that the product of a and b is 65/7, or ab = 65/7. Substituting 13/7 for b in this equation yields (a)(13/7) = 65/7. Dividing both sides of this equation by 13/7 yields a = 5.$qb$ from questions q where q.id = k.question_id and q.source_ref = 'CB-a45ffacb' and left(md5(q.stem), 8) = '32d35a8f';
update questions set stem = $qb$Function f is defined by f(x) = -a^(x) + b, where a and b are constants. In the xy-plane, the graph of y = f(x) - 15 has a y-intercept at (0, -99/7). The product of a and b is 65/7. What is the value of a?$qb$, image_url = null, updated_at = now() where source_ref = 'CB-a45ffacb' and left(md5(stem), 8) = '32d35a8f';
