update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$Choice B is correct. Let the measure of the third angle in the smaller triangle be a°. Since lines l and m are parallel and cut by transversals, it follows that the corresponding angles formed are congruent. So a° = y° = 20°. The sum of the measures of the interior angles of a triangle is 180°, which for the interior angles in the smaller triangle yields a + x + z = 180. Given that z = 60 and a = 20, it follows that 20 + x + 60 = 180. Solving for x gives x = 180 - 60 - 20, or x = 100.
Choice A is incorrect and may result from incorrectly assuming that angles x + z = 180. Choice C is incorrect and may result from incorrectly assuming that the smaller triangle is a right triangle, with x as the right angle. Choice D is incorrect and may result from a misunderstanding of the exterior angle theorem and incorrectly assuming that x = y + z.$qb$ from questions q where q.id = k.question_id and q.source_ref = 'CB-a6dbad6b' and left(md5(q.stem), 8) = '1bd3cb94';
