update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$Choice B is correct. The height of the tree at a given time is equal to its height when it was planted plus the number of feet that the tree grew. In the given equation, 14 represents the height of the tree at the given time, and 6 represents the height of the tree when it was planted. It follows that 2n represents the number of feet the tree grew from the time it was planted until the time it reached a height of 14 feet. Since n represents the number of years between the given time and the time the tree was planted, 2 must represent the average number of feet the tree grew each year.
Choice A is incorrect and may result from interpreting the coefficient 2 as doubling instead of as increasing by 2 each year. Choice C is incorrect. The height of the tree when it was 1 year old was 2(1) + 6 = 8 feet, not 2 feet. Choice D is incorrect. No information is given to connect the growth of one particular tree to the growth of similar trees.$qb$ from questions q where q.id = k.question_id and q.source_ref = 'CB-aa85b138' and left(md5(q.stem), 8) = '9fe9eed0';
