update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$Choice D is correct. It's given that the graph of the rational function f is shown, where y = f(x) and x ≥ 0. The graph shown passes through the point (3, 3). It follows that when the value of x is 3, the value of f(x) is 3. When the value of f(x) is 3, the value of f(x) + 5 is 3 + 5, or 8. Therefore, the graph of y = f(x) + 5 passes through the point (3, 8). Of the given choices, choice D is the only graph that passes through the point (3, 8) and is therefore the graph of y = f(x) + 5.
Choice A is incorrect. This is the graph of y = f(x) - 5, rather than y = f(x) + 5.
Choice B is incorrect. This is the graph of y = (f(x))/5, rather than y = f(x) + 5.
Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.$qb$ from questions q where q.id = k.question_id and q.source_ref = 'CB-aa95fb33' and left(md5(q.stem), 8) = 'a2db7e43';
