update question_options o set body = $qb$t = 2u/(u - 3)$qb$, image_url = null from questions q where q.id = o.question_id and o.label = 'D' and q.source_ref = 'CB-b03adde3' and left(md5(q.stem), 8) = '533bee61';
update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$Choice D is correct. Multiplying both sides of the given equation by t - 2 yields (t - 2)(u - 3) = 6. Dividing both sides of this equation by u - 3 yields t - 2 = 6/(u - 3). Adding 2 to both sides of this equation yields t = 6/(u - 3) + 2, which can be rewritten as t = 6/(u - 3) + (2(u - 3))/(u - 3). Since the fractions on the right-hand side of this equation have a common denominator, adding the fractions yields t = (6 + 2(u - 3))/(u - 3). Applying the distributive property to the numerator on the right-hand side of this equation yields t = (6 + 2u - 6)/(u - 3), which is equivalent to t = 2u/(u - 3).
Choices A, B, and C are incorrect and may result from various misconceptions or miscalculations.$qb$ from questions q where q.id = k.question_id and q.source_ref = 'CB-b03adde3' and left(md5(q.stem), 8) = '533bee61';
