update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$Choice A is correct. By distributing the minus sign through the expression (2/3 x - 5), the given expression can be rewritten as (1/2 x + 3) - 2/3 x + 5, which is equivalent to 1/2 x - 2/3 x + 3 + 5. Combining like terms gives (1/2 - 2/3) x + (3 + 5), or -1/6 x + 8.
Choice B is incorrect and may be the result of failing to distribute the minus sign appropriately through the second term and simplifying the expression 1/2 x + 3 - 2/3 x - 5. Choice C is incorrect and may be the result of multiplying the expressions (1/2 x + 3) and (-2/3 x + 5). Choice D is incorrect and may be the result of multiplying the expressions (1/2 x + 3) and (-2/3 x - 5).$qb$ from questions q where q.id = k.question_id and q.source_ref = 'CB-b47419f4' and left(md5(q.stem), 8) = '0bfab1d6';
