update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$Choice C is correct. It’s given that in a scale model, a length of 1 inch is equivalent to a length of 17/3 feet in the actual office building. This means that the ratio of a length, in feet, in the actual office building to the corresponding length, in inches, in the model is 17/3 to 1. Therefore, the length, in inches, in the model corresponding to a length in the actual office building of x feet can be found by dividing x by 17/3. Dividing by 17/3 is equivalent to multiplying by 3/17, so the corresponding length, in inches, in the model in terms of x can be represented by the expression 3x/17.
Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.
Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.
Choice D is incorrect. This expression represents the corresponding length, in inches, in the model in terms of x for a model where 1 inch in the model is equivalent to a length of 3/17, not 17/3, feet in the actual building.$qb$ from questions q where q.id = k.question_id and q.source_ref = 'CB-b5bc47d5' and left(md5(q.stem), 8) = 'c9423f4b';
