update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$Choice B is correct. Subtracting t from each side of the given equation yields 2r - t = 9s. Dividing each side of this equation by 9 yields (2r - t)/9 = s, which can be rewritten as s = (2r - t)/9. Therefore, the equation s = (2r - t)/9 correctly expresses s in terms of r and t.
Choice A is incorrect. This equation is equivalent to 2r = 9(s + t), not 2r = 9s + t.
Choice C is incorrect. This equation is equivalent to 2r = (s + t)/9, not 2r = 9s + t.
Choice D is incorrect. This equation is equivalent to 2r = s/9 + t, not 2r = 9s + t.$qb$ from questions q where q.id = k.question_id and q.source_ref = 'CB-b5ebd31c' and left(md5(q.stem), 8) = '9603d1bd';
