update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$The correct answer is 5. Dividing each side of the given equation by 3 yields x^(2) - 6x - 5 = 0. Adding 5 to each side of this equation yields x^(2) - 6x = 5. Therefore, if 3x^(2) - 18x - 15 = 0, the value of x^(2) - 6x is 5.$qb$ from questions q where q.id = k.question_id and q.source_ref = 'CB-c303ad23' and left(md5(q.stem), 8) = '230b21e9';
