update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$Choice B is correct. It's given that line s is parallel to line r in the xy-plane. This means that the slope of line r is equal to the slope of line s. Line r is defined by the equation 4x - 9y = 3. This equation can be written in slope-intercept form y = mx + b, where m represents the slope of the line and b represents the y-coordinate of the y-intercept of the line. Subtracting 4x from both sides of the equation 4x - 9y = 3 yields -9y = -4x + 3. Dividing both sides of this equation by -9 yields y = 4/9 x - 1/3. Therefore, the slope of line r is 4/9. Since parallel lines have equal slopes, the slope of line s is also 4/9.
Choice A is incorrect. This is the reciprocal of the slope of line s, not the slope of line s.
Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.
