update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$Choice B is correct. A linear function has a constant rate of change, and any two rows of the table shown can be used to calculate this rate. From the first row to the second, the value of x is increased by 2 and the value of f(x) is increased by 6 = 4 - (-2). So the values of f(x) increase by 3 for every increase by 1 in the value of x. Since f(2) = 4, it follows that f(2 + 1) = 4 + 3 = 7. Therefore, f(3) = 7.
