update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$Choice A is correct. The hematocrit can be expressed in terms of the blood volume and the plasma volume by solving the given equation V_B = (V_P)/(1 - H) for H. Multiplying both sides of this equation by (1 - H) yields V_B(1 - H) = V_P. Dividing both sides by V_B yields 1 - H = (V_P)/(V_B). Subtracting 1 from both sides yields -H = -1 + (V_P)/(V_B). Dividing both sides by -1 yields H = 1 - (V_P)/(V_B).
Choices B, C, and D are incorrect and may result from errors made when manipulating the equation.$qb$ from questions q where q.id = k.question_id and q.source_ref = 'CB-c77ef2fb' and left(md5(q.stem), 8) = '0c16ef53';
