update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$Choice B is correct. It’s given that in the equation 1/4xy + xyz = 1/3yz, x, y, and z are positive numbers. Multiplying both sides of this equation by the least common denominator of 12xyz yields 12xyz(1/4xy + xyz) = 12xyz(1/3yz), which gives 12xyz/4xy + 12x^(2)y^(2)z^(2) = 12xyz/3yz, or 3z + 12x^(2)y^(2)z^(2) = 4x. Subtracting 3z from both sides of this equation yields 12x^(2)y^(2)z^(2) = 4x - 3z. Dividing both sides of this equation by 12x^(2)z^(2) yields y^(2) = (4x - 3z)/(12x^(2)z^(2)). Taking the square root of both sides of this equation yields y = ±√((4x - 3z)/(12x^(2)z^(2))). Since y is a positive number, the expression √((4x - 3z)/(12x^(2)z^(2))) is equivalent to y.
Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.
Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.
Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.$qb$ from questions q where q.id = k.question_id and q.source_ref = 'CB-c8db0e19' and left(md5(q.stem), 8) = 'b3fc1133';
