update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$Choice D is correct. Adding 2/t to each side of the given equation yields 12/n = -2/w + 2/t. The fractions on the right side of this equation have a common denominator of tw; therefore, the equation can be written as 12/n = 2w/tw - 2t/tw, or 12/n = (2w - 2t)/tw, which is equivalent to 12/n = (2(w - t))/tw. Dividing each side of this equation by 2 yields 6/n = (w - t)/tw. Since n, t, w, and w - t are all positive quantities, taking the reciprocal of each side of the equation 6/n = (w - t)/tw yields an equivalent equation: n/6 = tw/(w - t). Multiplying each side of this equation by 6 yields n = 6tw/(w - t).
Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.
Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.
Choice C is incorrect. This is equivalent to 1/n rather than n.$qb$ from questions q where q.id = k.question_id and q.source_ref = 'CB-c8e9a011' and left(md5(q.stem), 8) = 'a22b9f73';
