update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$The correct answer is 18. Subtracting 45 from each side of the given equation yields |x - 9| = 18. By the definition of absolute value, if |x - 9| = 18, then x - 9 = 18 or x - 9 = -18. Adding 9 to each side of the equation x - 9 = 18 yields x = 27. Adding 9 to each side of the equation x - 9 = -18 yields x = -9. Therefore, the solutions to the given equation are 27 and -9, and it follows that the sum of the solutions to the given equation is 27 + (-9), or 18.$qb$ from questions q where q.id = k.question_id and q.source_ref = 'CB-c9417793' and left(md5(q.stem), 8) = 'ccde88e4';
