update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$Choice D is correct. It’s given that the measure of arc AB is 45° and the length of arc AB is 3 inches. The arc measure of the full circle is 360°. If x represents the circumference, in inches, of the circle, it follows that (45°)/(360°) = (3 inches)/(x inches). This equation is equivalent to 45/360 = 3/x, or 1/8 = 3/x. Multiplying both sides of this equation by 8x yields 1(x) = 3(8), or x = 24. Therefore, the circumference of the circle is 24 inches.
Choice A is incorrect. This is the length of arc AB.
