update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$Choice A is correct. The area, A, of a triangle is given by the formula A = 1/2 bh, where b is the length of the base of the triangle and h is the height of the triangle. In the right triangle shown, the length of the base of the triangle is 9 units, and its height is 4 units. Substituting 9 for b and 4 for h in the formula A = 1/2 bh yields A = 1/2 (9)(4), or A = 18. Therefore, the area of the triangle, in square units, is 18.
Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.
Choice C is incorrect. This is the length of the base of the triangle, in units, not the area of the triangle, in square units.
Choice D is incorrect. This is the height of the triangle, in units, not the area of the triangle, in square units.$qb$ from questions q where q.id = k.question_id and q.source_ref = 'CB-cab8f907' and left(md5(q.stem), 8) = '58b76d6c';
