update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$Choice D is correct. Each choice has a function with coefficient 5 and base 2, so the exponents must be analyzed. When the input value of x increases, the output value of f(x) decreases, so the exponent must be negative. An exponent of –x yields the values in the table: 5 = 5(2^(-0)), 5/2 = 5(2^(-1)), 5/4 = (2^(-2)), and 5/8 = 5(2^(-3)).
Choices A and B are incorrect and may result from choosing equations that yield an increasing, rather than decreasing, output value of f(x) when the input value of x increases. Choice C is incorrect and may result from choosing an equation that doesn’t yield the values in the table.$qb$ from questions q where q.id = k.question_id and q.source_ref = 'CB-dba7432e' and left(md5(q.stem), 8) = 'a2db7e43';
