update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$Choice C is correct. Using the distributive property to multiply the terms in the parentheses yields (2x^(3) · x^(3)) + (2x^(3) · -2x) + (3x · x^(3)) + (3x · -2x), which is equivalent to 2x^(6) - 4x^(4) + 3x^(4) - 6x^(2). Combining like terms results in 2x^(6) - x^(4) - 6x^(2).
Choices A and D are incorrect and may result from conceptual errors when multiplying the terms in the given expression. Choice B is incorrect and may result from adding, instead of multiplying, (2x^(3) + 3x) and (x^(3) - 2x).$qb$ from questions q where q.id = k.question_id and q.source_ref = 'CB-df0ef054' and left(md5(q.stem), 8) = '0bfab1d6';
