update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$Choice C is correct. Using the property that √x√y = √(xy) for positive numbers x and y, with x = (a + c)^(3) and y = a + c, it follows that √((a + c)^(3)) · √(a + c) = √((a + c)^(4)). By rewriting (a + c)^(4) as ((a + c)^(2))^(2), it is possible to simplify the square root expression as follows: √(((a + c)^(2))^(2)) = (a + c)^(2) = a^(2) + 2ac + c^(2).
Choice A is incorrect and may be the result of √((a + c)^(3)) ÷ √(a + c). Choice B is incorrect and may be the result of incorrectly rewriting (a + c)^(2) as a^(2) + c^(2). Choice D is incorrect and may be the result of incorrectly applying properties of exponents.$qb$ from questions q where q.id = k.question_id and q.source_ref = 'CB-e117d3b8' and left(md5(q.stem), 8) = 'f2d1f1df';
