update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$Choice B is correct. It's given that the speed of a vehicle is increasing at a rate of 7.3 meters per second squared. It's given to use 1 mile = 1,609 meters. There are 60 seconds in 1 minute; therefore, 60^(2) or 3,600 seconds squared is equal to 1 minute squared. It follows that the rate of 7.3 meters per second squared is equivalent to ((7.3 meters)/(1 second squared))((1 mile)/(1,609 meters))((3,600 seconds squared)/(1 minute squared)), or approximately 16.33 miles per minute squared. The rate, in miles per minute squared, rounded to the nearest tenth is 16.3.
Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.
Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.
Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.$qb$ from questions q where q.id = k.question_id and q.source_ref = 'CB-e7133228' and left(md5(q.stem), 8) = '027c3115';
