update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$Choice D is correct. It’s given that the graphs of x^(2) + y^(2) = 36 and y = mx + b/4, where m and b are negative constants, intersect at the point (-5, y) in the xy-plane. It follows that this intersection point represents a solution to the given system of equations. Substituting -5 for x in the equation x^(2) + y^(2) = 36 yields (-5)^(2) + y^(2) = 36, or 25 + y^(2) = 36. Subtracting 25 from each side of this equation yields y^(2) = 11. It's also given that y < 0, so taking the negative square root of each side of this equation yields y = -√11. Substituting -5 for x and -√11 for y in the equation y = mx + b/4 yields -√11 = m(-5) + b/4, or -√11 = -5m + b/4. Adding 5m to each side of this equation yields 5m - √11 = b/4. Multiplying each side of this equation by 4 yields 4(5m - √11) = b. Applying the distributive property to the left-hand side of this equation yields 20m - 4√11 = b. Therefore, the expression 20m - 4√11 represents the value of b.
Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.
Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.
Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.$qb$ from questions q where q.id = k.question_id and q.source_ref = 'CB-e833de9a' and left(md5(q.stem), 8) = '15c6bb10';
