update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$Choice B is correct. It’s given that y = 9(a/7)^(x + c) - b, where a, b, and c are positive constants such that a > 7 and b > c. The graph of any equation in the xy-plane crosses the x-axis when there is a point on the graph for which the value of y is equal to 0, and the value of y changes sign when the graph passes through that point. Since a > 7, the base a/7 is greater than 1, so the expression 9(a/7)^(x + c) - b increases as x increases. Since b is positive, there is a point on the graph of y = 9(a/7)^(x + c) - b for which the value of y is equal to 0. When the graph passes through this point, the value of y changes sign from negative to positive. Therefore, the graph of the given equation crosses the x-axis exactly one time.
Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.
Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.
Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.$qb$ from questions q where q.id = k.question_id and q.source_ref = 'CB-f01108a8' and left(md5(q.stem), 8) = 'f08a2c0a';
