update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$The correct answer is 565. In triangle XYZ, angle Y is a right angle. Therefore, triangle XYZ is a right triangle. The cosine of an acute angle in a right triangle is the ratio of the length of the side adjacent to that angle to the length of the hypotenuse. In right triangle XYZ, side YZ is the side adjacent to angle Z and side XZ is the hypotenuse. It’s given that the length of side YZ is 560 and the length of side XZ is 565. Therefore, cos Z = 560/565. It's also given that cos Z = 560/c. It follows that 560/c = 560/565. Therefore, c = 565.$qb$ from questions q where q.id = k.question_id and q.source_ref = 'CB-f1251f35' and left(md5(q.stem), 8) = 'd45e3aa4';
