Choices A, B, and D are incorrect and are the result of not understanding the relationships of the graphs of the two equations given. Choice A is incorrect because the two graphs intersect. Choice B is incorrect because in order for there to be only one intersection point, the horizontal line would have to intersect the parabola at the vertex, but the vertex is below the x-axis and the line is above the x-axis. Choice D is incorrect because a line cannot intersect a parabola in more than two points.$qb$ from questions q where q.id = k.question_id and q.source_ref = 'CB-f5247e52' and left(md5(q.stem), 8) = '46038b02';
