update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$The correct answer is 84. The sum of the measures of the interior angles of a triangle is 180°. It's given that in triangle JKL, the measures of ∠K and ∠L are each 48°. Adding the measures, in degrees, of ∠K and ∠L gives 48 + 48, or 96. Therefore, the measure of ∠J, in degrees, is 180 - 96, or 84.$qb$ from questions q where q.id = k.question_id and q.source_ref = 'CB-fd8745fc' and left(md5(q.stem), 8) = '8802539b';
