update question_keys k set explanation = $qb$Choice C is correct. It’s given that CD = EF and FC = DE, and the figure shows that D̅F̅ is a side of both △CDF and △EFD. Since △CDF and △EFD have three pairs of congruent sides, the triangles are congruent, where ∠CFD corresponds to ∠EDF and ∠CDF corresponds to ∠EFD. It’s given that the measure of ∠EDF is 65° and the measure of ∠EFD is 30°. Since corresponding angles of congruent triangles are congruent, ∠CFD is congruent to ∠EDF and ∠CDF is congruent to ∠EFD. Therefore, the measure of ∠CFD is 65° and the measure of ∠CDF is 30°. Since ∠CDE is made up of ∠CDF and ∠EDF, it follows that the measure of ∠CDE is equal to the sum of the measures of ∠CDF and ∠EDF. Therefore, the measure of ∠CDE is equal to (30 + 65)°, or 95°.
Choice A is incorrect. This is the measure of ∠CDF, not the measure of ∠CDE.
Choice B is incorrect. This is the measure of ∠CFD, not the measure of ∠CDE.
Choice D is incorrect. This is the sum of the measures of ∠CFD and ∠EDF, not ∠CDF and ∠EDF.$qb$ from questions q where q.id = k.question_id and q.source_ref = 'CB-ffc39dc5' and left(md5(q.stem), 8) = 'a2db7e43';
